# Terraform tests

- Tests live in `<module>/tests/<module>.tftest.hcl` and only use `command = plan`.
- Mock every provider the module uses (`azurerm`, `time`, `random`, `azuread`).
- `azurerm_client_config` must return UUIDs, or resources that validate IDs fail:

```hcl
mock_provider "azurerm" {
  mock_data "azurerm_client_config" {
    defaults = {
      tenant_id = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"
      object_id = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002"
    }
  }
}
```

- Use realistic ARM IDs for inputs such as subnet and zone IDs, because modules parse them with regex.
- Each module has:
  - one `run` asserting the secure defaults (public access, auth mode, zones, locks)
  - one `run` per feature toggle asserting its wiring (e.g. CMK role + encryption block)
  - negative `run`s with `expect_failures = [var.x]` or `[resource.address]` for validations and preconditions
- Assert on configuration values known at plan time, not on computed attributes.
- Run with `terraform init -backend=false && terraform test` or `scripts/check.sh <dir>`.
